{"run_id": "20260830T023734Z_baseline-s05-third-party-outage", "seq": 5, "ts": "2026-08-30T02:37:35.246Z", "type": "llm_response", "stop_reason": "stop", "text": "```json\n{\n  \"root_cause\": \"third_party_outage\",\n  \"service\": \"payments-api\",\n  \"action\": \"enable_circuit_breaker\",\n  \"target\": \"payments-api\",\n  \"confidence\": 1.0,\n  \"summary\": \"The third-party payment gateway (Paygate) is experiencing an outage and undergoing upstream maintenance, causing requests to timeout after 8 seconds. Enabling the circuit breaker on payments-api will prevent these long-running timeouts from degrading the api-gateway and exhausting resources.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    \"2026-08-30T02:50:32.000Z ERROR payments-api: paygate request timeout after 8000ms url=https://api.paygate.example/charges rid=ed4d2595\",\n    \"2026-08-30T02:52:04.000Z ERROR payments-api: paygate 503 Service Unavailable body='upstream maintenance' rid=0cf346e1\",\n    \"payments-api.latency_p95_ms: 114.881 123.106 7983.92 7960.08 8384.87\"\n  ],\n  \"report_markdown\": \"# Incident Report: Payments API Degradation due to Third-Party Outage\\n\\n### Summary\\nOn August 30, 2026, the `payments-api` service experienced a severe degradation with p95 latency spiking to over 8 seconds and error rates reaching 62%. This degradation cascaded to the `api-gateway`, causing 504 Gateway Timeouts for checkout requests. The root cause was identified as an outage/maintenance window at our third-party payment provider, Paygate.\\n\\n### Timeline\\n- **02:50:32 UTC**: First timeouts (8000ms) to `api.paygate.example` observed in `payments-api` logs.\\n- **02:52:04 UTC**: Paygate begins returning `503 Service Unavailable` with the body `'upstream maintenance'`.\\n- **02:58:00 UTC**: `api-gateway` and `payments-api` metrics show p95 latency jumping from ~120ms to >8000ms, and error rates spiking to ~62%.\\n- **03:12:00 UTC**: P1 alert fires for `payments-api` charge latency and failures.\\n\\n### Root Cause\\nThe external payment gateway (`Paygate`) is undergoing unscheduled upstream maintenance, leading to connection timeouts and 503 errors. Because the circuit breaker on `payments-api` is currently configured to `off`, the service continues to attempt connections and waits for the full 8-second timeout, exhausting gateway resources and degrading the user checkout experience.\\n\\n### Evidence\\n- **Logs**:\\n  - `ERROR payments-api: paygate request timeout after 8000ms url=https://api.paygate.example/charges`\\n  - `ERROR payments-api: paygate 503 Service Unavailable body='upstream maintenance'`\\n- **Metrics**:\\n  - `payments-api.latency_p95_ms` spiked from `123.106` to `7983.92` and remained around `8000ms`.\\n  - `payments-api.error_rate_pct` spiked from `0.4%` to `62%`.\\n\\n### Remediation\\n1. **Enable Circuit Breaker**: Update the configuration of `payments-api` to set `CIRCUIT_BREAKER` to `on`. This will allow the service to fail fast, preventing cascading latency issues on the `api-gateway`.\\n2. **Escalate to Vendor**: Contact Paygate support to get an ETA on their upstream maintenance completion.\\n\\n### Follow-ups\\n- Implement automatic circuit-breaking thresholds for all third-party integrations.\\n- Review and align the `api-gateway` upstream timeout (currently 5000ms) with downstream timeouts to prevent unnecessary resource holding.\"\n}\n```", "output_ref": null, "tool_calls": [], "output_tokens": 952, "latency_ms": 22712, "input_tokens": 20659, "cached": true, "provider": "gemini"}
